WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.100
Let’s walk through Activity.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.112
Use the activity feed as a triage surface.

00:00:05.112 --> 00:00:08.500
Open the native destination behind a notice before responding,

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.050
because the badge tells you that something changed but does

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:13.725
not provide the complete decision context.

00:00:13.725 --> 00:00:16.762
On this slide, review newly submitted records, deck

00:00:16.762 --> 00:00:20.887
changes, proposal rounds, and White Cell communications.

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:24.363
In practice, the badge signals unread activity;

00:00:24.363 --> 00:00:27.200
opening a notice should take you to its native destination

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.488
before you act.

00:00:28.985 --> 00:00:31.910
When you are ready, use Open Activity to move

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:33.385
to the live surface.

00:00:33.385 --> 00:00:36.085
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:36.085 --> 00:00:36.235
.
